TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed checkpoint cp-build at stage checkpoint:record because the worklist-fixed command `bash container/build.sh` rewrites the tracked file results/receipts/build.json, so the driver rejected the run for changing tracked files instead of validating the prepared base. Evidence: the gate node for cp-build recorded verdict pass with exit code 0, so the build command itself succeeded; the worktree diff against base 71f2beb shows only results/receipts/build.json modified in place (ts 07:07:21Z -> 10:59:43Z, wall_clock_s 839 -> 1, image_digest sha256:175edc16... -> sha256:e678f60e...). The cause is in the source, not in the checkpoint: container/build.sh's write_receipt() unconditionally writes $REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/build.json, and that path is tracked — commit c1363cb (container-recipe) committed the receipt, while .gitignore covers only results/logs/, not results/receipts/. Worse, a local podman build carries no registry digest, so the script falls back to the image Id, which changes on every rebuild; the committed receipt therefore can never be reproduced byte-for-byte by a re-run, and no ordering, caching, or environment change available inside this checkpoint can make the command leave the tree clean. This is systemic rather than specific to cp-build: cp-weights, cp-smoke, cp-tp2 and cp-bench run receipt-producing scripts (scripts/stage-weights-both.sh, scripts/run-smoke.sh, scripts/run-tp2.sh, bench/run-matrix.sh) against the same tracked results/receipts/ directory and will fail the same way, and results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json are tracked for the same reason. The result-projection-timeout in the failure detail (finalMessage capture for adapter spec-build-driver not projected within 10000 ms) is a downstream consequence of the driver aborting at checkpoint:record, not an independent machinery or session fault, so this is not transient. The remedy is a source fix outside this checkpoint's authority — receipts are per-run artifacts and must be untracked and ignored, exactly as results/logs/ already is, with scripts/receipts-verify.py already treating missing receipts as legal — hence blocked; checkpoint tasks are non-retryable by contract in any case.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":[".gitignore","results/receipts/build.json","results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json","results/receipts/weights-worker.json"],"goal":"Make generated receipts untracked run artifacts so that receipt-producing checkpoint commands leave the tracked worktree clean. Add results/receipts/*.json to .gitignore (alongside the existing results/logs/ entry), keep results/receipts/.gitkeep as the only tracked entry under results/receipts/ so the directory still exists in a fresh clone, and remove the three currently committed receipts from the index with `git rm --cached` (leaving any on-disk copies in place). Do not change container/build.sh's receipt contents or the receipt schema, and do not weaken scripts/receipts-verify.py, which already documents that missing receipts are legal and that a present receipt must be well-formed. After this change, `bash container/build.sh` and the other receipt-producing scripts write into an ignored directory, `git status --porcelain` stays empty across a run, and checkpoint cp-build can be re-dispatched against the prepared base.","acceptance":[{"id":"receipts-index-clean","description":"The only tracked path under results/receipts/ is the .gitkeep placeholder; no generated receipt JSON remains in the git index.","argv":["bash","-euc","[ \"$(git ls-files results/receipts)\" = \"results/receipts/.gitkeep\" ]"]},{"id":"gitkeep-still-tracked","description":"results/receipts/.gitkeep is still tracked so the receipts directory exists in a fresh clone.","argv":["bash","-euc","git ls-files --error-unmatch results/receipts/.gitkeep"]},{"id":"receipts-ignored","description":"Generated receipt JSON files under results/receipts/ are matched by .gitignore.","argv":["bash","-euc","git check-ignore -q results/receipts/build.json && git check-ignore -q results/receipts/weights-worker.json"]},{"id":"receipt-write-leaves-tree-clean","description":"Writing a receipt JSON into results/receipts/ does not dirty the tracked worktree, which is the condition the checkpoint driver enforces.","argv":["bash","-euc","mkdir -p results/receipts; printf '{}\\n' > results/receipts/_probe.json; s=\"$(git status --porcelain)\"; rm -f results/receipts/_probe.json; test -z \"$s\""]},{"id":"receipts-verify-passes","description":"The receipts gate still passes with receipts absent or present, confirming missing receipts remain legal.","argv":["python3","scripts/receipts-verify.py"]},{"id":"packaging-tests-pass","description":"The packaging test suite that container/build.sh runs first still passes.","argv":["python3","-m","unittest","discover","-s","tests"]}],"dependencies":["container-recipe"]}}
